Subject: [PATCH] XR: fence netdevice forwarding mutations before PPE binding

Move the AP32 bridge forwarding fence to net/core so bridge and netdevice
writers share one writer count and generation. Cover the full MTU, MAC
address, upper link/unlink, close (through NETDEV_DOWN), flag change, netns
move and unregister scopes, including rejection and rollback paths, instead
of pairing pre/post notifier events. Bridge port removal and every bridge
MAC/ID change are fenced as well. L2 templates also require egress MTU to
cover ingress MTU. NPU/PPE opt-ins remain disabled.

